# SPEC-2026-032 — Schedules por partido (7 eventos)

**Estado:** Implementado — ver `docs/issues/SPEC-2026-032-match-lifecycle-schedules.md`. Activar con `enable_match_schedules` + `provision_match_schedules.py`.

## Resumen

Al **dar de alta** o **actualizar** `kickoff_utc` de un partido → provisionar schedules **one-time** en EventBridge Scheduler (nombres determinísticos). Al borrar/replace → `deprovision_match`.

| # | Evento | Offset (vs kickoff) | Lambda |
|---|--------|---------------------|--------|
| 1 | Trivia pre-partido | **−2 h** | `trivia_pre_match_dispatcher` |
| 2 | Reminder #1 (sin pred.) | **−1 h** | `match_reminder_dispatcher` |
| 3 | Reminder #2 (sin pred.) | **−30 min** | `match_reminder_dispatcher` |
| 4 | Reminder #3 (sin pred.) | **−15 min** | `match_reminder_dispatcher` |
| 5 | Veda | **−5 min** | `veda_activator` |
| 6 | Resultados | **+110 min** | `result_collector` (`match_ended`) |
| 7 | Scoring | Tras (6) | `scoring_processor` vía SQS `FINISH_MATCH` (+ catch-up opcional +120 min) |

**Hoy:** `ingest_matches` solo escribe DynamoDB — **no** crea schedules.

## Nombres (idempotentes)

`trivia-pre-{match_id}`, `remind-60-{match_id}`, `remind-30-{match_id}`, `remind-15-{match_id}`, `veda-{match_id}`, `result-{match_id}`, `scoring-catchup-{match_id}` (opcional).

## Componente nuevo

`src/services/scheduler_manager.py` → `MatchScheduleManager.provision_match | update_kickoff | deprovision_match`

Hooks: `MatchDAO.put_match`, `ingest_matches`, `sync_fixture_from_api`.

